Description:

What is claimed is: 1. A method comprising:receiving at a receiver a compressed media signal representative of a scenewherein the compressed media signal is formed by compressing a media signal based on a sensing matrix that is determined using a sensing matrix template and a set of template parameterswherein the sensing matrix is a product of a first random matrix template and a second matrix the set of template parameters comprises a first random number generator seed and the sensing matrix is a product of a first random matrix and the second matrix andwherein the first random matrix is determined using the first random matrix template and a sequence of random numbers generated using the first random number generator seed;receiving a specification of a subset of the set of template parameters wherein the media signal cannot be reconstructed from the compressed media signal using the subset of the set of template parameters; andextracting at least one scene descriptor representative of at least one portion of the scene from the compressed media signal using the sensing matrix template and the subset of the set of template parameters. 2. The method of claim 1 wherein the at least one scene descriptor is at least one of an object descriptor and a motion descriptor. 3. The method of claim 1 wherein the media signal comprises a video signal. 4. The method of claim 1 further comprising:determining the first random matrix template based on at least one of a random circulant transform a locally randomized discrete Fourier transform or a random convolution transform. 5. The method of claim 1 wherein the second matrix comprises exactly one non-zero entry in each row and wherein indices of the non-zero entries in rows of the second matrix are selected based on a number of shifted values of indices that equal other indices of the non-zero entries in rows of the second matrix. 6. The method of claim 1 further comprising:receiving the set of template parameters in response to detection of an anomaly that indicates that the receiver is to reconstruct the media signal from the compressed media signal. 7. The method of claim 6 further comprising:reconstructing the media signal from the compressed media signal using the set of template parameters selectively provided to the receiver. 8. A method comprising:generating at a server a set of sensing matrix template parameters that is used to specify a sensing matrix by applying it to a sensing matrix template;providing the set of sensing matrix template parameters to a media acquisition device for compression of a media signal representative of a scene based on the sensing matrix template; andselectively providing a subset of the set of sensing matrix template parameters to a receiver that is configured to receive the compressed media signal from the media acquisition devicewherein the media signal cannot be reconstructed from the compressed media signal using the subset of the set of sensing matrix template parameterswherein the sensing matrix is a product of a first random matrix template and a second matrix the set of sensing matrix template parameters comprises a first random number generator seed and the sensing matrix is a product of a first random matrix and the second matrix andwherein the first random matrix is determined using the first random matrix template and a sequence of random numbers generated using the first random number generator seed. 9. The method of claim 8 wherein the receiver is able to extract at least one scene descriptor representative of at least one portion of the scene from the compressed media signal using the sensing matrix template and using knowledge of the subset of the set of sensing matrix template parameters. 10. The method of claim 9 wherein the at least one scene descriptor is at least one of an object descriptor and a motion descriptor. 11. The method of claim 8 wherein the media signal comprises a video signal. 12. The method of claim 8 wherein selectively providing the subset of the set of sensing matrix template parameters comprises providing a specification of a random sequence to the receiver in response to detecting an anomaly that indicates that the receiver is to reconstruct the media signal from the compressed media signal using the random sequence. 13. The method of claim 8 further comprising:determining the first random matrix template based on at least one of a random circulant transform a locally randomized discrete Fourier transform or a random convolution transform. 14. The method of claim 8 wherein the second matrix comprises exactly one non-zero entry in each row and wherein indices of the non-zero entries in rows of the second matrix are selected based on a number of shifted values of indices that equal other indices of the non-zero entries in rows of the second matrix. 15. A receiver comprising:a transceiver configured to receive a compressed media signal representative of a scene wherein the compressed media signal is formed by compressing a media signal based on a sensing matrix that is determined using a sensing matrix template and a set of template parameters wherein the sensing matrix is a product of a first random matrix template and a second matrix the set of template parameters comprises a first random number generator seed and the sensing matrix is a product of a first random matrix and the second matrix and wherein the first random matrix is determined using the first random matrix template and a sequence of random numbers generated using the first random number generator seedwherein the transceiver configured to receive a specification of a subset of the set of template parameters wherein the media signal cannot be reconstructed from the compressed media signal using the subset of the set of template parameters; anda processor configured to extract at least one scene descriptor representative of at least one portion of the scene from the compressed media signal using the sensing matrix template and the subset of the set of template parameters. 16. The receiver of claim 15 wherein the at least one scene descriptor is at least one of an object descriptor and a motion descriptor. 17. The receiver of claim 15 wherein:the processor is configured to determine the first random matrix template based on at least one of a random circulant transform a locally randomized discrete Fourier transform or a random convolution transform. 18. The receiver of claim 15 wherein the second matrix comprises exactly one non-zero entry in each row and wherein indices of the non-zero entries in rows of the second matrix are selected based on a number of shifted values of indices that equal other indices of the non-zero entries in rows of the second matrix. 19. The receiver of claim 15 wherein:the transceiver is configured to receive the set of template parameters in response to detection of an anomaly that indicates that the receiver is to reconstruct the media signal from the compressed media signal. 20. The receiver of claim 19 wherein:the processor is configured to reconstruct the media signal from the compressed media signal using the set of template parameters selectively provided to the receiver.

